Round-2 findings are written to `collab/1791600000000-reviewer-srvm-phase4a-r2.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md`.

**Verdict: READY_TO_MERGE.** The source is byte-identical to the reviewed commit and correct by reading. All five confirmation points hold:

1. **Item 8 is now discriminating.** The test pins every precondition literally (saved window `{1 vector}`, frame rd 2, body result register 0, three-key callee window) and asserts the exact post-return map, so a program change cannot re-vacuate it silently. I re-derived the vector and both mutant windows; they match the failures the orchestrator and codex observed.
