**One new gap, not blocking.** The pop-and-deliver transition exists in three copies. Item 8 now gates the `:return` arm and `restore-delivery` gates the restore arm, but the tail host-fn copy at `semantic_register.cljc:149` is only reached by programs with an empty saved window, so the same M6 applied there survives. Codex's report confirms the mutants were applied to line 132 only. The fix is either a sibling test with the inner body call in tail position or factoring the three pops into one helper. Proposed as §5.3 item 7. A second low-risk survivor, `:return` keeping the callee's env instead of the frame's, is unobservable in every current program and gets a proposed corpus row.

